Fixtures of the AMR reader tests.

sample2_nb.amr, dtx_nodata_nb.amr: real AMR-NB files from https://samples.ffmpeg.org/A-codecs/amr/
  (sample2.amr; amrnb-dtx-nodata/amrnb-dtx-nodata.amr, which has SID (FT 8) and NO_DATA (FT 15)
  frames). Redistributed as FFmpeg's FATE sample set.
sine_nb.amr: generated with ffmpeg (libopencore_amrnb, 12.2 kbit/s) from a 440 Hz sine tone.
*.3gp: `ffmpeg -c copy -f 3gp` remuxes of the .amr/.awb file of the same name (samr/sawb tracks
  with a damr box).
synthetic_wb.awb, synthetic_nb_mc2.amr, synthetic_wb_mc3.awb: generated by a script (seed 4867): valid
  headers and TOC bytes of all file frame types with random payloads, as no AMR-WB encoder is
  available. The multi-channel files have the channel description of RFC 4867 section 5.2 (2 and 3
  channels). They test framing only, they are not decodable audio.
